From a7bc57150bf29f15de3c7534726d9c20ff544740 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: opencode <opencode@local>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 19:56:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] sycl: serve block_size 1024 in the Hadamard fast path

llama_mul_mat_hadamard() reshapes the activation to [block_size, K] and
multiplies it by a block_size x block_size rot, so every MUL_MAT tagged
GGML_HINT_SRC0_IS_HADAMARD by prism.hadamard folding presents n == block_size.
The switch only covered 64/128/256/512, which are the KV-cache sizes, so
block_size 1024 fell through to a dense matmul against a 4 MiB rot tensor
that was re-read and re-multiplied per folded weight.

Sylvester H is symmetric, so the register-resident FWHT already used for the
smaller sizes computes exactly rot^T * res; the existing 1/sqrt(n) at load
gives 1/32 at n=1024. No new code path, one case.

Measured on Arc Pro B70, Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-PTQ1_0, 256-token decode,
median of 3: 25.04 -> 26.27 tok/s, arithmetic canary exact.
---
 ggml/src/ggml-sycl/fwht.cpp | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/fwht.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/fwht.cpp
index 2312b3d13..6e5374421 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/fwht.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/fwht.cpp
@@ -113,6 +113,16 @@ bool ggml_sycl_op_fwht(ggml_backend_sycl_context & ctx, const ggml_tensor * src,
         case 512:
             launch_fwht<512>(src_d, dst_d, rows, scale, stream);
             return true;
+        // Ternary-Bonsai weight rotation. llama_mul_mat_hadamard() reshapes the
+        // activation to [block_size, K] and multiplies it by a block_size x
+        // block_size rot, so a hinted MUL_MAT from prism.hadamard folding always
+        // presents n == block_size. At block_size 1024 the 4 MiB rot tensor is
+        // otherwise re-read and re-multiplied as a dense matmul per folded weight.
+        // Sylvester H is symmetric, so the FWHT result is bit-comparable to
+        // rot^T * res up to the same 1/sqrt(n) the smaller cases already apply.
+        case 1024:
+            launch_fwht<1024>(src_d, dst_d, rows, scale, stream);
+            return true;
         default:
             return false;
     }
